description:
Specified by CONTRIBUTING.md § Releasing (Alberto's ruling 2026-09-23; see fleet-gr4). .github/workflows/release.yml, on push to main:
1. read the version from Cargo.toml (every crate agrees); refuse if tag v<x.y.z> exists or the version does not match the merged release/ or hotfix/ branch;
2. refuse if the branch carries no docs release pass (a commit whose subject says 'docs release pass for <x.y.z>');
3. tag v<x.y.z>;
4. changelog: the release branch's commit subjects between main's previous release and the branch tip, one line per item (full id plus what), beads and version-bump commits left out; from the PR's commit list, since the squash hides them on main;
5. create the GitHub release with that changelog (gh release create);
6. publish docs/ for the version (the renderer is undecided; until then, attach docs/ to the release as an archive and say so).

Open for the builder: whether release binaries (macOS arm64 at least) are built and attached, which the demo's 'try it tonight' wants (fleet-adz.7, the 0.1.0 install script in build.md).

Done when: a dry run on a scratch release (e.g. a v0.0.1-test tag on a fork or with workflow_dispatch) produces the release, the changelog and the docs artifact, and a release without a docs pass is refused.
